  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answers:</strong> <b>Configure a recipe that modifies the configuration file and attach it to the Configure lifecycle event for the targeted web layer.</b> and <b>Create a recipe that sets up the configuration file and link it to the Deploy lifecycle event of the web layer.</b></p> <p>To ensure a configuration file is ready <strong>before</strong> launching your web application, you need to create a custom recipe that provisions or updates this configuration file. In AWS OpsWorks, you can attach recipes to lifecycle events—<b>Configure</b> and <b>Deploy</b> being the most appropriate here. By hooking into these events, you guarantee your configuration is established at the right time during instance setup or application deployment.</p> <p><em>Update the stack to utilize AWS-maintained cookbooks</em> is incorrect, as AWS built-in cookbooks do not cater to your custom configuration file needs, nor do they offer the flexibility required for your scenario. <em>Switch the stack to use custom cookbooks</em> by itself does not fulfill the requirement—it simply enables custom cookbooks, but you must still define and associate a recipe to an appropriate lifecycle event. Thus, the main steps are <b>writing</b> the recipe to create/manage the config file and <b>attaching</b> it to either the Configure or Deploy event for the relevant web layer.</p> <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Recipes linked to the Configure event run during setup and configuration changes; those on the Deploy event execute before application deployment. Use the event most suitable for when your config file must be available.</p>",
  "query": "<p>You are the DevOps Engineer at your organization. The team is leveraging an OpsWorks stack to provision several web servers. It is necessary to provision a configuration file <strong>before</strong> the hosted web application launches on new instances. What actions should you take to satisfy this requirement? Select <strong>two</strong> from the following choices:</p>",
